For the past ten days or so, I've been encountering a problem that I've never had in Markor v2.15.2 in years of use. Basically, if I have a link written in my txt file on my Galaxy A54, Markor doesn't recognize it as a link, so a double-tap doesn't recognize which app should open that link. Example:
<screenshot below>
Here I noticed three strange behaviors, all related:
1. When I had a link on Markor, I just had to double-tap on the link for Markor to select the entire link.
2. After selecting it, to the left of the three lines, I had the icon of the app that should have opened the link. I clicked on that icon and Markor took me to the app.
3. For 10 days, none of this has been working, and I am encountering the problem, so I am forced to double-tap on the link, then press the three lines icon to select the entire link, then paste the link into another text editor in order to open the link

All this despite the fact that I haven't updated Markor in the last 10 days (the last update was 4 months ago from F-Droid, automatic) and despite the fact that I haven't changed any settings. Can you help me solve this, please? Thank you.

